.TH HALT 8 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
halt \- stop the system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halt
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-p | \-r ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default
.B halt
asks
.BR init
(process 1) to shut the system down by sending it
.BR SIGTERM .
.B halt
returns as soon as the signal has been delivered; it does not wait for
the shutdown to finish.
.PP
On receipt of the signal init terminates login sessions, runs
.BR "/etc/rc stop" ,
sends
.B SIGHUP
and
.B SIGTERM
to every remaining process, waits up to five seconds, sends
.BR SIGKILL ,
writes a shutdown record to
.IR /var/log/wtmp ,
calls
.BR sync (2),
and finally calls
.BR reboot (2)
with
.BR RB_HALT_SYSTEM .
.PP
If signalling init fails,
.B halt
prints a warning and falls back to calling
.BR reboot (2)
itself.
.PP
Both paths require an effective user ID of 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Do not signal init; call
.BR reboot (2)
directly.
Processes are not terminated and
.B /etc/rc stop
is not run, although the kernel still unmounts all file systems
before the machine goes down.
.TP
.B \-p
Power off instead of halting: signal init with
.B SIGUSR1
or, with
.BR \-f ,
call
.BR reboot (2)
with
.BR RB_POWER_OFF .
Equivalent to
.BR poweroff (8).
.TP
.B \-r
Reboot instead of halting: signal init with
.B SIGUSR2
or, with
.BR \-f ,
call
.BR reboot (2)
with
.BR RB_AUTOBOOT .
Equivalent to
.BR reboot (8).
.PP
If both
.B \-p
and
.B \-r
are given, the last one wins.
Each option must be given as a separate argument; combined forms
such as
.B \-fp
are rejected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Init was signalled, or
.BR reboot (2)
returned without error.
.TP
.B 1
.BR reboot (2)
failed (for example with
.B EPERM
when not run as root).
.TP
.B 2
An unrecognized argument was given; a usage message is printed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rc
Run by init with the argument
.B stop
during an orderly shutdown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kill (2),
.BR reboot (2),
.BR sync (2),
.BR poweroff (8),
.BR reboot (8)
.SH BUGS
The kernel does not implement a true halt:
.B RB_HALT_SYSTEM
is handled exactly like
.BR RB_AUTOBOOT ,
so
.B halt
resets the machine instead of stopping it.
